,{"type":"Cross-link","start":953,"end":953,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2)"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":973,"end":973,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2)"},{"type":"Site","start":984,"end":985,"description":"Cleavage; by CASP6"},{"type":"Region","start":984,"end":1198,"description":"Autoinhibitory domain (AID)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":992,"end":992,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1041,"end":1041,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1155,"end":1155,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1188,"end":1188,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":1191,"end":1191,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO)"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with CREB1, SIAH1, WSB1, CBX4, TRADD, p53/TP53, TP73, TP63, CREBBP, DAXX, P53DINP1, SKI, SMAD1, SMAD2 and SMAD3, but not SMAD4. Interacts with ATF1, PML, RUNX1, EP300, NKX1-2, NKX2-5, UBE2I, HMGA1, CTBP1, AXIN1, NLK, MYB, POU4F1, POU4F2, POU4F3, UBE2I, UBL1 and ZBTB4. Probably part of a complex consisting of p53/TP53, HIPK2 and AXIN1. Interacts with SP100; positively regulates TP53-dependent transcription. Interacts with SUMO1P1/SUMO5 (PubMed:27211601). Interacts with DAZAP2; the interaction results in phosphorylation of DAZAP2 which causes localization of DAZAP2 to the nucleus, reduces interaction of DAZAP2 with HIPK2 and prevents DAZAP2-dependent degradation of HIPK2 (PubMed:33591310). Interacts with SIAH1; the interaction is promoted by DAZAP2 and results in SIAH1-mediated ubiquitination and subsequent proteasomal degradation of HIPK2 (PubMed:33591310)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with Hantaan hantavirus nucleoprotein"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with Seoul hantavirus nucleoprotei